  "codex_reviewed_caveats": {
    "anova_interpretation": "F(6,5)=6.87, p=0.026 is exploratory, not confirmatory. N=14 with 6 dummies + 2 covariates + intercept leaves residual dof=5. One or two extreme firms (esp. the fabless pair) can drive F. Treat as directional signal only.",
    "fabless_cherry_pick": "K1106b fabless pair (MediaTek, Realtek) both strongly negative, but K1104 4-firm fabless sample had mixed signs: MediaTek -1.61e-3, Realtek -2.39e-3, Novatek +7.02e-4, Phison +1.20e-3. H2 should be read as \"fabless is bimodal, not uniformly negative\"; K1104 broader regression is more reliable for fabless inference.",
    "consumer_split": "Pres. Chain (2912) theta2=+5.22e-4 (t=+2.92); Uni-President (1216) theta2=-3.29e-5 (t=-6.17 but tiny effect). Consumer defensive does not exhibit a clean sector-level pattern; this is firm-specific information-discovery not sector effect.",
    "shipping_h3_rejected": "Evergreen -3.62e-5, Wanhai +5.38e-5; mean near zero. Freight rate shocks do NOT translate to earnings-day vol amplification. Likely because Baltic Dry / SCFI are real-time public info so earnings add little incremental vol-relevant news.",
    "electronics_single_point": "Hon Hai (2317) theta2=+7.25e-4 t=+3.59 is the highest in this sample and replicates K1104 exactly. But n=1 for electronics so no sector-level claim possible. Needs Quanta/Asus to form a sector.",
    "replicability_note": "10 firms overlap with K1104; all 10 show Delta=0.0% because the single-shot MLE is deterministic and the parquet cache was shared. This confirms methodology reproducibility."
  }
